Author: matiasrodriguezc01 <matiasrodriguezc01@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 15 21:51:52 2026 -0300

    Fix empty chunk content for documents over 1000 chars
    
    IndexingService.chunkDocument replaced every chunk's content with ''
    when the source document exceeded 1000 characters. Q&A scores chunks
    by keyword overlap, so these documents never matched (or produced
    empty excerpts), giving fallback answers with no useful citations.
    
    Chunks now always keep their paragraph text. Adds a vitest regression
    test covering import -> index -> ask on the sample documents (fails
    before the fix, passes after) and a vitest.config.ts so tests run from
    the repo root instead of vite.config.ts's src/renderer root.
    
    Note: previously indexed documents keep their empty chunk files until
    reindexed (startIndexing skips docs already listed in index-meta.json).

